WEBVTT

00:00.480 --> 00:05.530
<b>III</b>

00:00.480 --> 00:05.530
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

00:00.480 --> 00:05.530
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

00:03.450 --> 00:06.500
<i>It's been three days since 
Nanahoshi collapsed.</i>

00:07.350 --> 00:11.550
<i>She's still unresponsive, and we don't 
know why she coughed up blood.</i>

00:12.290 --> 00:18.290
<i>Yuruzu of Atonement has the power 
to transfer health and vigor,</i>

00:18.290 --> 00:21.080
<i>and it sounds like he 
can cure most diseases.</i>

00:21.870 --> 00:26.530
<i>Sylphie is convinced Nanahoshi 
collapsed because of her magic.</i>

00:27.330 --> 00:32.250
<i>She feels responsible, and she won't 
let anyone else help with the cure.</i>

00:32.250 --> 00:36.670
<i>I hope Nanahoshi gets better soon, 
for both their sakes. Still...</i>

00:38.880 --> 00:41.320
Well, Karowante?

00:41.320 --> 00:45.440
She bears no trace of external 
interference apart from detoxification.

00:45.830 --> 00:49.690
The flow of mana in her 
body appears stagnant,

00:49.690 --> 00:51.020
but I cannot say why.

00:51.540 --> 00:53.280
Search the archives, then.

00:53.280 --> 00:54.200
Yes, sire!

00:54.460 --> 00:56.170
I... I'll help.

00:56.170 --> 01:00.400
No. I'll have no outsiders 
in my archives.

01:08.200 --> 01:10.620
Do you think Nanahoshi will get better?

01:11.190 --> 01:14.150
All is as great Millis wills it.

01:19.280 --> 01:25.050
<i>I once saw a movie where aliens came 
to Earth and a cold wiped them out.</i>

01:26.380 --> 01:29.070
<i>Is she gonna die?</i>

01:32.780 --> 01:35.730
We have determined the nature 
of Ms. Nanahoshi's malady.

01:36.200 --> 01:37.760
She has Dryne Syndrome.

01:38.270 --> 01:43.630
It dates to a long-ago time when people 
possessed far less mana than now.

01:44.030 --> 01:50.290
Those unable to neutralize mana entering 
their bodies died without exception.

01:50.290 --> 01:51.790
Or so the records say.

01:51.790 --> 01:55.930
That does seem to match 
what Nanahoshi's going through.

01:56.520 --> 01:58.180
Is there a cure?

01:58.380 --> 01:59.780
I do not know.

01:59.780 --> 02:02.500
It says only that the disease

02:02.500 --> 02:06.190
was eradicated 7,000 years ago, 
as people's mana grew stronger.

02:06.480 --> 02:10.810
<i>That's around the time of the 
First Human-Demon War.</i>

02:11.460 --> 02:13.680
So, what are you going to do?

02:13.680 --> 02:19.070
I will command Scarecoat of Time 
to halt its flow for Nanahoshi.

02:19.070 --> 02:23.450
Those on the surface may seek 
a cure in the meantime.

02:23.720 --> 02:27.370
Surely Your Majesty's influence 
could help with that?

02:27.370 --> 02:30.700
Nanahoshi and I have 
merely struck a bargain.

02:30.700 --> 02:34.840
I will not place myself in 
someone's debt to save her.

02:36.310 --> 02:38.330
Do not mistake me.

02:38.330 --> 02:42.110
She is my guest. 
I will do the minimum to save her.

02:42.580 --> 02:45.050
But I will not do the maximum.

02:45.050 --> 02:51.490
I live only to find and defeat Laplace 
when he eventually rises again.

02:51.710 --> 02:53.760
<i>Laplace will "rise again"?</i>

02:53.760 --> 02:56.600
<i>You mean that seal on 
him won't hold forever?</i>

02:56.600 --> 02:59.580
What will happen when he does return?

02:59.580 --> 03:05.860
Knowing him, he will lead the demons in 
another attempt to destroy humankind.

03:08.090 --> 03:10.630
<i>Basically, since he's got 
his eye on that prize,</i>

03:10.630 --> 03:14.130
<i>he'll only go so far out 
of his way to help us.</i>

03:14.130 --> 03:16.130
You mean you'd abandon Nanahoshi?!

03:16.470 --> 03:18.760
I said no such thing.

03:18.760 --> 03:23.370
That's a lie! I know someone of 
your stature could find a cure!

03:24.970 --> 03:28.150
Ability does not entail obligation.

03:28.150 --> 03:32.430
The hell it doesn't! 
The strong have a duty to help the weak!

03:33.400 --> 03:36.810
Don't impose the odious 
creed of Millis on me.

03:36.810 --> 03:37.950
What did you say?!

03:37.950 --> 03:41.020
You're talking about throwing 
Nanahoshi to the wolves!

03:41.390 --> 03:42.990
If you're going to help, 
see it through to the—

03:42.990 --> 03:43.740
Stop!

03:44.440 --> 03:47.010
I understand how you feel, 
but restrain yourself.

03:47.370 --> 03:50.690
I don't want to lose you 
over something like this.

03:57.910 --> 04:01.530
If you have objections, 
I suggest you take action.

04:01.530 --> 04:04.090
Surely your god says as much.

04:04.090 --> 04:08.180
"Depend not on others to 
render aid," I believe?

04:11.890 --> 04:14.150
<i>I want to save Nanahoshi.</i>

04:14.150 --> 04:17.320
<i>Still, even Perugius has limits.</i>

04:17.560 --> 04:20.220
<i>But then, what can I possibly do?</i>

04:24.570 --> 04:25.830
By your leave.

04:27.360 --> 04:30.170
Ms. Nanahoshi has regained consciousness.

04:37.730 --> 04:39.190
Are you okay?

04:43.580 --> 04:45.840
Do I look okay?

04:50.480 --> 04:54.600
They told me... 
they can't cure what I've got.

04:54.600 --> 04:59.000
But it's not incurable. 
We just don't know how to treat it!

04:59.000 --> 05:02.230
Precisely. We need only find a cure.

05:02.230 --> 05:04.420
You mustn't lose heart.

05:03.570 --> 05:09.740
<i>Stock reassurances are the last thing 
someone in real pain wants to hear.</i>

05:04.420 --> 05:09.330
Despairing when you're not well 
will only make recovery harder.

05:12.880 --> 05:15.240
I don't know what to say.

05:28.950 --> 05:34.250
I guess I wasn't the healthiest 
person to begin with.

05:34.930 --> 05:41.370
I wasn't getting sick <i>all</i> the time, 
but I had a bad cold at least once a year.

05:41.980 --> 05:46.370
And medicine hasn't advanced 
much in this world, you know?

05:46.370 --> 05:51.370
I know they've got magic, 
but they don't even clean cuts.

05:52.000 --> 05:56.520
Lots of people end up 
dying because of that.

05:56.520 --> 05:57.920
Silly, right?

05:59.910 --> 06:07.010
I've been really careful since 
I found out I couldn't do magic.

06:07.500 --> 06:10.250
I figured, if I got sick,

06:11.440 --> 06:15.500
I'd probably never get better again.

06:16.260 --> 06:20.050
Anyway, this world just makes no sense.

06:20.050 --> 06:23.510
The whole thing ignores 
the laws of physics.

06:23.770 --> 06:29.410
I mean, even I thought it was 
neat when I first got here.

06:30.010 --> 06:32.400
I'd be lying if I said

06:32.400 --> 06:36.630
I wasn't excited to be in 
a sword-and-sorcery world.

06:45.170 --> 06:48.540
I don't want to die. 
Not in a place like this!

06:49.620 --> 06:51.090
I don't want to die!

06:51.090 --> 06:53.960
I don't want to die in this crazy world!

06:54.280 --> 06:56.170
Why should I?! It makes no sense!

06:56.590 --> 07:00.780
Hey! Did you know I haven't 
changed at all in eight years?!

07:00.780 --> 07:03.190
I don't get taller, 
and even my hair stays the same!

07:03.190 --> 07:06.640
I get hungry, and I eat and poop,

07:06.640 --> 07:09.020
but my nails don't grow, 
and I never get my period!

07:09.020 --> 07:11.870
I'm not from this world!

07:11.870 --> 07:13.780
I can't live here!

07:13.780 --> 07:15.930
I'm like a corpse!

07:16.850 --> 07:19.770
So, why...

07:20.610 --> 07:23.870
Why do I still have to get sick?!

07:25.690 --> 07:27.490
What sense does that make?!

07:27.490 --> 07:30.920
Why do I have to go through this?!

07:31.310 --> 07:32.890
I don't want to die!

07:32.890 --> 07:37.180
I... I don't want to die 
in this perverse world!

07:37.180 --> 07:41.300
I mean, I've never even kissed anyone!

07:41.300 --> 07:44.800
I have a crush, but I never 
even got to say, "I love you!"

07:44.010 --> 07:44.800
C-Calm down—

07:44.800 --> 07:47.070
I envy you, you know?!

07:47.450 --> 07:50.380
You always seem happy! You've got a life!

07:50.380 --> 07:51.730
What's your problem?!

07:51.730 --> 07:53.360
Your dad died?!

07:53.360 --> 07:56.110
Your mom's sick?!

07:56.110 --> 07:58.710
So what?! You're the lucky one!

07:58.710 --> 08:03.180
I won't even be there when my dad dies, 
the way things are going!

08:03.180 --> 08:07.390
I could die here, and my mom
 would never even know!

08:08.240 --> 08:13.840
I want to see them—see my mom and dad.

08:18.990 --> 08:22.810
I remember that morning.

08:23.770 --> 08:28.190
My dad said he'd be home early that day.

08:29.420 --> 08:34.140
My mom said she'd cook 
Pacific saury for dinner.

08:34.720 --> 08:40.310
I told my dad not to hurry 
because I'd have friends over,

08:40.810 --> 08:45.330
and I grumbled at my mom 
that I was sick of saury.

08:45.930 --> 08:48.660
Why did I act like that?!

08:49.450 --> 08:53.710
I bet they're both worried sick about me.

08:54.630 --> 08:56.320
I want to see them.

08:56.320 --> 08:57.720
I want to go home.

08:58.320 --> 09:00.310
I don't want to die.

09:00.310 --> 09:03.410
I don't want to die here.

09:08.470 --> 09:11.600
<i>"I want to go home." 
"I want to see my family."</i>

09:11.600 --> 09:17.620
<i>I bet that wouldn't have meant much 
to me when I first came to this world.</i>

09:18.240 --> 09:20.420
<i>Now, though, I get it.</i>

09:21.090 --> 09:24.320
<i>I know how much just living 
with family can mean</i>

09:24.750 --> 09:26.910
<i>and how scary it is to lose that.</i>

09:27.970 --> 09:33.350
<i>If anything threatened my home life, 
I'd fight to the death to protect it.</i>

09:34.060 --> 09:40.670
<i>Maybe I've been all Nanahoshi's had 
to comfort her. A reminder of Japan.</i>

09:41.240 --> 09:47.000
<i>Something to help her feel connected 
to that world and the life she lost.</i>

09:47.530 --> 09:50.560
Somebody... help me.

10:01.350 --> 10:02.630
What is it?

10:02.630 --> 10:03.980
I'm going to do something.

10:04.250 --> 10:09.630
I would appreciate any support you can 
give without compromising your duty.

10:09.630 --> 10:13.130
Oh? You'll "take action," will you?

10:17.650 --> 10:18.890
Very well.

10:18.890 --> 10:23.070
I could not bear to watch 
Nanahoshi die, either.

10:23.070 --> 10:24.560
Thank you.

10:25.140 --> 10:30.120
Not to rush things, sire, but could 
you contact Dragon God Orsted?

10:30.120 --> 10:31.510
I cannot.

10:31.770 --> 10:35.010
And he appeared a century or so ago.

10:35.010 --> 10:40.170
For all his knowledge, he would hardly 
know of a 7,000-year-old illness.

10:40.560 --> 10:41.880
I see.

10:42.160 --> 10:44.960
<i>Wait. Seven thousand years old?</i>

10:45.460 --> 10:49.280
In that case, could you send 
me to the Demon Continent?

10:49.280 --> 10:52.660
The Demon Continent? 
What will you do there?

10:54.130 --> 10:58.650
I'd like to visit the Great Emperor of 
the Demon World, Kishirika Kishirisu.

10:59.600 --> 11:02.760
<i>The Great Emperor of the 
Demon World, Kishirika Kishirisu.</i>

11:02.760 --> 11:05.300
<i>The person who gave me 
the Eye of Foresight.</i>

11:05.620 --> 11:07.820
<i>Believe it or not, the history books say</i>

11:07.820 --> 11:09.440
<i>she was at the center of</i>

11:09.440 --> 11:12.940
<i>the Human-Demon Wars 
that started 7,000 years ago.</i>

11:13.240 --> 11:18.180
<i>I'll track her down and ask her about 
a cure. That's the plan, anyway.</i>

11:18.580 --> 11:23.190
The problem is, our target wanders 
all over the Demon Continent.

11:23.190 --> 11:25.490
That makes finding her a challenge.

11:25.490 --> 11:27.890
Who knows how many months it could take?

11:27.890 --> 11:32.700
Even so, I'd like you all 
to help me save Nanahoshi.

11:32.700 --> 11:37.470
In that case, 
I will outfit you for your journey.

11:37.470 --> 11:39.040
Thank you very much.

11:39.450 --> 11:43.350
Zanoba, Elinalise, I'd like you 
to come with me as bodyguards.

11:43.350 --> 11:44.990
I am your man, Master!

11:44.990 --> 11:46.260
I'd be happy to.

11:46.780 --> 11:47.940
I'll go with you!

11:48.550 --> 11:52.480
I can understand Nanahoshi's longing 
for her homeland as well as anyone!

11:52.480 --> 11:55.720
Let me go! I want to do 
something to help her!

11:56.000 --> 11:57.070
Please!

11:59.330 --> 12:00.490
All right.

12:00.490 --> 12:01.530
You mean it?

12:01.530 --> 12:03.770
Yes. I'd appreciate your help.

12:03.770 --> 12:04.900
Count on it.

12:05.130 --> 12:07.600
What should I do?

12:07.600 --> 12:11.770
I'd like you to stay here for a bit and 
recover from Nanahoshi's treatment.

12:11.770 --> 12:13.620
Okay. Then what?

12:13.880 --> 12:15.740
Once you're done recuperating...

12:17.750 --> 12:21.670
I'd like you to go home 
and take care of Lucie.

12:22.750 --> 12:25.690
I might not be able to 
make it home for a while,

12:25.690 --> 12:30.390
and I don't think it's good for a baby 
to go without parents that long.

12:32.190 --> 12:34.870
Okay. You do have a point.

12:35.290 --> 12:39.850
I'll need to keep an eye on 
Lucie if you're going to be gone.

12:39.850 --> 12:41.070
Sorry.

12:41.070 --> 12:42.230
Don't be.

12:42.620 --> 12:46.620
You've done plenty, Sylphie. 
Let us take it from here.

12:47.230 --> 12:48.040
Okay.

12:48.650 --> 12:51.860
But don't lose your
 other arm or anything.

12:52.360 --> 12:53.970
I'll do my best.

12:55.090 --> 12:56.250
What?!

12:56.250 --> 12:58.370
You're going on another long trip?

12:58.370 --> 12:59.930
Manners, Aisha.

12:59.930 --> 13:02.080
But, Mom...

13:02.080 --> 13:05.230
I plan to come home every so often.

13:06.170 --> 13:08.840
<i>I've got Perugius on my side this time.</i>

13:08.840 --> 13:11.100
<i>That means almost zero travel time.</i>

13:11.400 --> 13:13.690
<i>I can come home any time, no problem.</i>

13:14.460 --> 13:16.860
Take care, Brother.

13:16.860 --> 13:20.350
Thanks. Keep up with your 
student council work.

13:20.350 --> 13:21.460
I will.

13:27.370 --> 13:29.740
Well then, watch the 
place while I'm gone.

13:29.740 --> 13:32.030
The house is safe with us.

13:32.030 --> 13:35.250
Best of luck, Master Rudeus.

13:35.710 --> 13:36.750
Thank you.

13:41.910 --> 13:46.440
Oh! I never dreamed there was 
another such chamber below ground.

13:46.800 --> 13:53.220
King Perugius believes this circle will 
bring you nearest to the Demon Emperor.

13:53.220 --> 13:57.520
You mean King Perugius has an idea 
where to find Emperor Kishirika?

13:57.520 --> 13:59.140
Naturally.

13:59.140 --> 14:04.020
But we are not certain how things 
stand there. Be careful.

14:04.020 --> 14:07.310
Well, we'll turn around 
if things get dicey.

14:08.230 --> 14:09.870
Take care.

14:09.870 --> 14:10.800
We will.

14:15.790 --> 14:18.870
Okay. Go, Zanoba Robo! Open that door!

14:18.870 --> 14:20.610
Yes, Master!

14:23.970 --> 14:27.250
By the by, Master. What is a "robo"?

14:27.250 --> 14:32.660
It's a regional term for a mighty 
man with a body like steel.

14:32.660 --> 14:36.320
I see. Your knowledge never 
fails to impress, Master.

14:37.080 --> 14:39.540
So, this is the Demon Continent!

14:42.230 --> 14:48.100
Be careful, Cliff. It's home to a lot 
of large and dangerous monsters.

14:48.370 --> 14:50.090
Yeah, I know.

14:50.450 --> 14:53.930
And I doubt you'll find many 
followers of Millis here.

14:53.930 --> 14:56.670
Try not to pick fights 
if you can help it.

14:56.670 --> 14:58.670
I don't need you to tell me—

14:59.160 --> 15:01.440
No, you're right. I'll be careful.

15:01.770 --> 15:05.880
We don't speak Demon-God, 
so that won't be a problem.

15:05.880 --> 15:07.680
Oh, right.

15:08.270 --> 15:09.400
Master!

15:10.810 --> 15:12.260
Do you see something?

15:19.890 --> 15:22.610
<i>This</i> is where he meant?

15:22.880 --> 15:29.370
<i>I've been here with Eris and Ruijerd, 
and it didn't leave a great impression.</i>

15:29.900 --> 15:31.510
<i>We're in Rikarisu.</i>

15:36.910 --> 15:37.790
Huh?

15:38.120 --> 15:39.410
Halt.

15:39.410 --> 15:40.540
Is there a problem?

15:40.540 --> 15:42.920
Nah. We just need to check the woman.

15:47.790 --> 15:49.040
Can I help you?

15:49.250 --> 15:50.090
What do you think?

15:50.090 --> 15:51.010
Hm...

15:54.540 --> 15:58.820
<i>She doesn't </i>not<i> look like Elinalise, 
but there's a big power gap.</i>

15:58.820 --> 16:00.400
<i>I won't say where, though.</i>

16:00.390 --> 16:03.100
It's not her. You can go.

16:03.100 --> 16:04.440
Has there been some kind of trouble?

16:04.440 --> 16:07.520
Nothing you need to know about.

16:07.760 --> 16:10.350
I assume they're looking for someone.

16:10.350 --> 16:12.010
It seems like it.

16:34.030 --> 16:35.630
Thank you for waiting.

16:36.160 --> 16:37.990
What do we do now?

16:37.990 --> 16:43.520
If Perugius is right, 
someone here may have seen Kishirika.

16:43.520 --> 16:45.240
We'll start by asking around—

16:44.770 --> 16:46.270
Hey, there!

16:46.270 --> 16:48.690
Long time no see!

16:48.690 --> 16:51.440
You're looking great!

16:53.870 --> 16:55.830
<i>He's the guy who—</i>

16:56.490 --> 16:59.410
Not traveling with Roxy anymore?

16:59.410 --> 16:59.960
<i>Huh?</i>

16:59.960 --> 17:03.760
Oh, you were in Roxy's 
old party, weren't you?

17:03.760 --> 17:04.370
<i>Huh?</i>

17:04.370 --> 17:05.920
<i>Wait, what?</i>

17:05.920 --> 17:08.320
<i>Elinalise, I need details!</i>

17:08.320 --> 17:11.210
Rudeus, interpret for us.

17:11.210 --> 17:13.680
This gentleman knows Roxy.

17:14.210 --> 17:19.760
I'm Nokopara. Do you speak my language?

17:20.890 --> 17:23.180
Yes, Nokopara.

17:23.180 --> 17:26.270
I speak Demon-God.

17:26.270 --> 17:31.420
He's quite knowledgeable about this city. 
Why not ask for his help?

17:31.420 --> 17:32.890
We might as well.

17:33.610 --> 17:36.740
I'm Quagmire. It's a nice to meet you.

17:36.740 --> 17:38.530
Quagmire, huh?

17:38.530 --> 17:42.490
Have we met somewhere?

17:42.490 --> 17:44.200
No, I doubt it.

17:44.200 --> 17:46.040
We're looking for someone.

17:46.040 --> 17:47.370
Would you lend us a hand?

17:47.370 --> 17:50.130
How much will you pay?

17:50.290 --> 17:53.670
Two green ore coins.

17:53.670 --> 17:55.300
And if you find her...

17:55.300 --> 17:57.880
how's another two sound?

17:57.880 --> 18:01.890
Four green ore coins?!
Y-You sure you wanna go that high?!

18:01.890 --> 18:04.640
That shows how big a hurry we're in.

18:04.640 --> 18:09.020
But don't get any funny ideas
just because we have money.

18:09.020 --> 18:15.860
Hey, now!
Like I'd ever trick a friend of Roxy's!

18:15.860 --> 18:17.740
You're in good hands!

18:19.710 --> 18:22.640
Now, what do you say we get looking, too?

18:32.490 --> 18:34.130
<i>So much for my bright idea.</i>

18:34.550 --> 18:39.010
<i>I didn't count on Jalil and 
Vizquel being long gone.</i>

18:39.010 --> 18:41.420
I'm terribly sorry, Master.

18:41.420 --> 18:43.700
If only we could speak Demon-God as well.

18:43.700 --> 18:45.010
Don't worry about it.

18:45.310 --> 18:47.640
There you are.

18:48.560 --> 18:51.900
I got some good info for you.

18:52.560 --> 18:57.450
See, the Demon King's looking for

18:57.450 --> 18:59.700
the Great Emperor of the Demon World, too.

18:59.700 --> 19:01.660
Really?

19:01.660 --> 19:06.540
Yup. Since about a year ago.

19:06.540 --> 19:10.250
That Demon King wouldn't happen to be

19:10.250 --> 19:12.420
named Badigadi, would he?

19:12.420 --> 19:15.040
Nah, not King Badi.

19:15.040 --> 19:17.800
His big sis, King Atofe.

19:17.800 --> 19:21.680
Who knew that Badi had a big sister?

19:21.680 --> 19:25.680
In that case, why don't we ask King Atofe?

19:25.680 --> 19:27.930
Wh-Whoa. Don't even think about it.

19:27.930 --> 19:30.770
King Atofe is bad news.

19:30.770 --> 19:33.310
You'd best steer clear of her.

19:33.310 --> 19:34.600
Really?

19:35.850 --> 19:37.180
Is something wrong?

19:37.180 --> 19:39.320
I could do with a bite to eat.

19:39.580 --> 19:42.230
I'll get enough for everyone over there.

19:42.230 --> 19:43.690
I'll go with you.

19:43.690 --> 19:45.240
Take care.

19:47.940 --> 19:50.400
Oh, Master. What did you learn?

19:50.400 --> 19:52.990
Something about a Demon King who—

19:53.310 --> 19:55.090
Wait, where are Cliff and Elinalise?

19:55.090 --> 19:58.590
They went that way to procure food.

19:58.590 --> 20:00.010
Oh, okay.

20:02.840 --> 20:08.400
Master, you needn't feel responsible 
for Nanahoshi's condition.

20:08.400 --> 20:09.630
I guess not.

20:10.020 --> 20:15.980
Of course, even I know something 
of her desire to return home.

20:15.980 --> 20:18.190
That is why I'm here to help.

20:18.190 --> 20:19.480
Really?

20:19.480 --> 20:22.780
I thought you liked the 
life you have now.

20:23.010 --> 20:24.810
I do, naturally,

20:24.810 --> 20:30.170
but I also find myself pining 
for the sights of my homeland.

20:30.170 --> 20:33.740
Nanahoshi must have left 
something precious in hers,

20:33.740 --> 20:37.740
given her desperation to return to it.

20:38.420 --> 20:41.790
Her crush and her family. 
At least, that's what she told me.

20:42.340 --> 20:46.430
I'm afraid both those reasons 
are rather lost on me.

20:46.710 --> 20:48.920
They're like figures are to you.

20:49.300 --> 20:53.280
I see. They must mean a 
great deal to her, then.

20:54.980 --> 20:56.270
Ugh! You reek!

20:56.270 --> 20:57.440
You're filthy!

20:57.440 --> 21:00.980
Food... Won't someone offer me food?

21:00.980 --> 21:02.650
Don't come near me.

21:02.650 --> 21:04.320
You stink!

21:04.320 --> 21:05.650
Forget it!

21:10.220 --> 21:12.330
Here. Eat up.

21:12.330 --> 21:14.690
Thank you! Thank you!

21:15.860 --> 21:16.960
Delicious!

21:16.960 --> 21:19.420
Delicious! Great! Tasty!

21:19.420 --> 21:21.710
<i>Huh? Why am I getting déjà vu?</i>

21:21.710 --> 21:25.960
Scrumptious!

21:32.170 --> 21:34.820
You have my thanks.

21:34.820 --> 21:36.430
Y-You're welcome.

21:36.430 --> 21:38.820
I am...

21:38.820 --> 21:42.170
Kishirika Kishirisu!

21:42.170 --> 21:45.040
They call me...

21:45.450 --> 21:49.420
the Great Emperor of the Demon World!

21:50.330 --> 21:51.210
That's me!

21:53.030 --> 21:54.550
That's me!

21:55.030 --> 21:57.900
I owe you my life!

21:57.900 --> 21:58.830
So,

21:58.830 --> 22:01.920
I shall grant you one wish!

22:01.920 --> 22:03.950
I'm waiting!

22:01.920 --> 22:04.920
<b>Episode 9
Lament</b>

23:34.930 --> 23:39.960
Next Time
An Audience with an Immortal Demon King
